open scoped GoFV.SSA.Sem.Fixed

/-!
# Non-vacuity witness: slice G29 of the genssa validator on `type:.eq.M1K1M2`

`test/genmeth1/main/.eq.M1K1M2,1.ssa` and `…,1.prog` of the corpus
`gofv-corpus/2aae1000ea1d/quick-v10/plain`, embedded verbatim (`fSsa`, `fProg`): the
compiler-generated equality of a struct with a byte at offset 0 and a `uint16` at offset 2.

`checkG28` rejects it (`MOVDnop/MOVDreg: upper bits unknown`); `checkG29` accepts it with the PC
table `tab` and the class table `kt`. Block `b5` (the bytes agree) loads the two halfwords
(`v26 = MOVHUload` into `R2`, `v31 = MOVHUload` into `R1`) and widens them (`v21 = MOVDnop v26`,
`v33 = MOVDnop v31`, no code) for the `CMPW`. Before `v33` (index 3), G20's one-entry table `uAt`
is empty (it names only the previous value's load), while G29's table `uL` still has `v31`'s
entry `(1, 16, false)`, carried across `v21`: `R1` is zero-extended from 16 bits.

By compiled evaluation (`native_decide`, listed in `scripts/axioms-allowlist.txt`; `g29_facts`),
`stepLoc` runs `v33` from a state with the 16-bit integer `0xbeef` in `R1` and the 32-bit integer
`0x1234` in `R2` to `R1 = 0xbeef` as a 32-bit integer. On a framed activation with `G28Env`, from
a machine whose `X1` and `X2` are zero-extended from 16 bits (`UOKL` of `uL` before `v33`),
`g29_value` runs `v33`, and the table after it gives the whole `X1 = 0xbeef`
(`genG29_value_witness`).
-/

